From dc8b40ac15940f957021c448a15b5c8654b293a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Mar 2026 22:13:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bdev/kvmalloc: add a malloc-like bdev that supports the KV command set

Add a new bdev module that implements an in-memory key-value store
using a red-black tree. Supports KV STORE, RETRIEVE, DELETE, EXIST,
and LIST operations via NVMe I/O passthru.

The module also handles NVMe admin passthru for KV-specific identify
commands (CNS 0x05 and 0x06), allowing upper layers to discover KV
namespace and controller capabilities without requiring KV-specific
fields on the generic bdev layer.

Change-Id: I24736dd9cce0d33310a7072aa390b9d3ec591323
Signed-off-by: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
---

